@vmittal-msft @YatishSVC @sdszhang — requesting review when you have a chance.

This fixes the silent PFC queue-group mismatch tracked in #26174: the framework assumed 8 PFC TX queue groups per tgen port, while newer high-speed load modules honor only 4 — pause frames for priorities mapped above queue 3 were silently ignored, causing intermittent pause-storm test failures. The framework now resolves the size from the connected ports once per session (testbed override > detected > default 8) and logs the deciding source; existing testbeds with the override configured are unaffected, and non-IxNetwork backends keep today's behavior.

Validated on a 4x400G testbed — detection and override paths both exercised (logs in the PR description). Related context: the same mismatch was the root cause behind the traffic-rate workaround removed from #25950.
